762 0 obj
  << /ActualText (In 2023\054 I joined the Royal Bank of Canada engagement as a consultant leading UX design strategy for an ambitious project called RBC Clear\054 which entailed designing and building an entirely new application from the ground up\056\n\nThe design team for this engagement was small\054 but when I joined\054 they had already developed an initial design system with several pages\056 With my technical background\054 I owned both the Accounts section and the Developer Portal\056 The first focused on a suite of experiences that enabled CFOs at large enterprise companies to manage all their accounts in one place\054 while the latter provided a space for CTOs and developers to access APIs for implementation into their own products\056 Both spaces had very specific user needs with little overlap between the two\056\n\nWithin this case study\054 I will walk through the end\055to\055end process we developed\054 as well as the journey we went on\054 leading to the launch of the app and the awards it won as a result\056)
     /K [ 8 ]
     /P 763 0 R
     /Pg 746 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

763 0 obj
  << /K [ 762 0 R ]
     /P 802 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 746 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

764 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Redefining the design process)
     /K [ 9 ]
     /P 765 0 R
     /Pg 746 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

765 0 obj
  << /K [ 764 0 R ]
     /P 802 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 746 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

766 0 obj
  << /ActualText (One of the challenges the team was facing when I first joined the project was a misalignment between product management and design\056 This often meant that new requirements were only identified at the approval stage rather than during discovery\054 forcing designs to be reworked late in the process\056 After investigating further\054 I identified that one of the root causes of this issue was a lack of standardization in the end\055to\055end process from business requirements to design to development\054 in addition to an unclear understanding of how product management and design work together\056\n\nTo alleviate the issue\054 increase team efficiency\054 and improve collaboration with stakeholders\054 I developed a standardized process that plugged into the already established service design approach\056 This new process involved\072\n\nWorkshop sessions with key stakeholders\054 led by designers\054 to develop a complete product Service Design Blueprint\056\nBlueprint reviews where designers and product managers together identify user tasks and add them to a task list\056\nTask mapping where the designer turns the identified tasks into Task Flow Diagrams\054 which are then verified with stakeholders\056\nLow\055fidelity designs built from the diagrams to receive approval from executive leadership before creating and delivering the high\055fidelity designs\056)
     /K [ 10 ]
     /P 767 0 R
     /Pg 746 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

767 0 obj
  << /K [ 766 0 R ]
     /P 802 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 746 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

